Hi Igor,

My mail of 11 September was wrong. I withdraw it.

I wrote that the 102 induced resets and the all-0x80 buffer were not
yours. They are yours. You reported both on 25 August in the v9 02/13
thread: the inference after the forced autosuspend that "succeeded" and
returned all 48 output channels uniformly 128, and "in 102 induced
resets across nine runs today it appeared only on the arm that does not
carry them". The v10 cover was quoting you, and quoting you correctly,
six days later.

The 45 resets of 19 August and the 102 of 25 August are two different
runs, both yours, and neither contradicts the other. I read only the
19 August thread, did not find the 102 in it, and concluded it had been
invented. I should have searched for it before saying in public that
you had not measured it.

Nothing in the series changes. Both of your Tested-by lines stand as you
sent them, and what 4/14 says about the 19 August differential is still
accurate.

Jiaxing
